Subject: [PATCH] RPCEnvironment: skip confirmation-password re-auth for API tokens

reauth_user_for_user_modification requires the caller to provide their own
password as a confirmation before modifying a user. This is a sensible
interactive-session safeguard, but API tokens are already authenticated by
the token secret — requiring a password re-confirmation makes tokens
unable to perform user modifications at all.

This patch detects when the authuser is an API token (user@realm!tokenname)
and skips the password re-authentication in that case. The normal ACL
permission checks (Realm.AllocateUser + User.Modify) still apply and must
pass before this function is reached.

--- a/usr/share/perl5/PVE/RPCEnvironment.pm
+++ b/usr/share/perl5/PVE/RPCEnvironment.pm
@@ reauth_user_for_user_modification:
-    # Regular users need to confirm their password to change TFA settings.
-    if ($authuser ne 'root@pam') {
-        raise_param_exc({ $param_name => 'password is required to modify user' })
-            if !defined($password);
-
-        ($authuser, my $auth_username, my $auth_realm) =
-            PVE::AccessControl::verify_username($authuser);
-
-        my $domain_cfg = PVE::Cluster::cfs_read_file('domains.cfg');
-        my $cfg = $domain_cfg->{ids}->{$auth_realm};
-        die "auth domain '$auth_realm' does not exist\n" if !$cfg;
-        my $plugin = PVE::Auth::Plugin->lookup($cfg->{type});
-        $plugin->authenticate_user($cfg, $auth_realm, $auth_username, $password);
-    }
+    # Regular users need to confirm their password to change TFA/user settings.
+    # API tokens are already authenticated by the token secret — skip re-auth.
+    if ($authuser ne 'root@pam') {
+        my (undef, $token_name) = PVE::AccessControl::split_tokenid($authuser, 1);
+        if (!defined($token_name)) {
+            raise_param_exc({ $param_name => 'password is required to modify user' })
+                if !defined($password);
+
+            ($authuser, my $auth_username, my $auth_realm) =
+                PVE::AccessControl::verify_username($authuser);
+
+            my $domain_cfg = PVE::Cluster::cfs_read_file('domains.cfg');
+            my $cfg = $domain_cfg->{ids}->{$auth_realm};
+            die "auth domain '$auth_realm' does not exist\n" if !$cfg;
+            my $plugin = PVE::Auth::Plugin->lookup($cfg->{type});
+            $plugin->authenticate_user($cfg, $auth_realm, $auth_username, $password);
+        }
+    }
